From a26664f6051c51eb870822efab1fcfa7a60dced8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhruvan <kartd01@purdue.edu>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:35:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [targets] add __int128 on 32-bit i386, ARM, RISC-V,
 PowerPC and MIPS o32 - hasInt128Type() is true on X86_32, ARM, RISCV32, PPC32
 (not AIX) and   MIPS o32, so __int128, __int128_t and __SIZEOF_INT128__ exist
 without   -fforce-enable-int128, with the layout that flag gives (size 16,
 align 16) - CodeGenModule's data-layout consistency check (asserts builds)
 skips   __int128 on 32-bit targets, as it already did under the flag: ARM,
 RV32,   PPC32 and MIPS data layouts have no i128 entry (alignment 8) -
 compiler-rt builtins: -fforce-enable-int128 on i386/i686/arm*/thumb*/  
 powerpc/powerpcspe/mips/mipsel under clang, so the ti builtins  
 (CRT_HAS_128BIT) are always built there. Every one of these backends   calls
 __floattidf/__fixdfti and friends for i128<->fp; PowerPC and MIPS   also call
 __divti3/__umodti3. Mul, shifts and (elsewhere) division expand   inline. -
 tests: new CodeGen/Preprocessor/Sema kairo-int128-32bit.c; updated the  
 tests that asserted __int128 was missing on these targets (128bitint.c,  
 Driver/types.c, atomic-ops.c, builtins-arm-exclusive.c,  
 builtins-ppc-quadword.c, mips-type-sizes-int128.c, Frontend/int128.cpp,  
 microsoft-vs-float128.cpp)

ABI note: libc++ keys on __SIZEOF_INT128__, so on i686 and armv7 (and the
others) std::filesystem::file_time_type becomes duration<__int128> and
extra __int128 formatter instantiations appear (Kairo ticket P605). A
libc++ built by a compiler without this patch is not link-compatible with
code built by one with it: every already-built sysroot for these targets
must be rebuilt by the patched compiler (ksys builds libc++ and user code
with the same compiler, so a fresh sysroot is consistent).
